    "id": "monster_mimic_chair",
    "type": "monster",
    "name": "Mimic Chair",
    "source_section": "M8. DINING ROOM, p.6",
    "full_text": "The reason for the odd number of chairs is that the chair closest to the door to area M6 is a mimic that escaped from area M19. It moved the real chair to the corner and took its place, hoping to capture any creature entering from the kitchen. It has been able to ambush only the occasional cat or faerie dragon, so it's in a weakened state and has the following changes to its stat block:\n• It has 30 hit points.\n• The DC to escape its grapple is 10.",
    "summary": "A mimic disguised as a chair near the door from area M6. It ambushes creatures entering from the kitchen, but is weakened with only 30 HP and a lower DC to escape its grapple.",
    "keywords": [
      "mimic",
      "chair"
